Package: openlivegamer4k-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: DKMS kernel driver for the AVerMedia Live Gamer 4K (GC573)
 Source-only V4L2 capture driver for the AVerMedia Live
 Gamer 4K (GC573, PCI 1461:0054) HDMI capture card, with concurrent
 stereo 48 kHz LPCM capture through ALSA.
 .
 This package installs the driver source and registers it with DKMS,
 which builds and installs the kernel module for each kernel with
 matching headers. Installation is NOT capture-ready: the module
 requires explicit first-use options (bridge_link, bridge_bootstrap,
 reset_gpio_mask and related values) that must be supplied on the
 first module load. See README.Debian for the activation command,
 next-boot behavior, and rollback guidance.
 .
 Beta prerelease. Intended targets: Ubuntu 24.04 (Noble) and Linux Mint
 22.x on amd64, with kernels whose headers are installed. Tested on Linux
 Mint 22.3, kernel 6.17.0-22-generic; Ubuntu 24.04 is intended but untested.

Package: openlivegamer4k-control
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, python3, alsa-utils, psmisc, pkexec
Recommends: openlivegamer4k-dkms (= ${source:Version})
Description: GTK4 control app for the OpenLiveGamer4K GC573 capture driver
 Native X11/Wayland (GTK 4) desktop app to inspect the AVerMedia Live
 Gamer 4K (GC573) V4L2 node and preview HDMI capture.
 .
 Read-only device status by default, safe to run while OBS or another
 V4L2 client owns the node. Preview is an explicit user action that
 takes the exclusive node and releases it on stop; it never preempts
 another client. The app runs unprivileged, has no network or telemetry,
 and still launches when no card is present (it reports the device is
 absent).
 .
 This package does not require the openlivegamer4k-dkms driver package
 to install or start; it installs independently.
